WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.480
Global Config holds shared framework configuration, credential references

00:00:04.693 --> 00:00:05.952
and provider settings.

00:00:06.187 --> 00:00:09.600
Choose the intended vault mode and verify its runtime support.

00:00:10.027 --> 00:00:12.141
Keep vault material and backups protected.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:16.562
Credential groups now organize local definitions by datacenter and cluster,

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.253
with shared-service groups for references used across environments.

00:00:20.595 --> 00:00:23.803
Use search and purpose labels to find the intended reference.

00:00:24.153 --> 00:00:26.898
Local secret values remain masked in the list.

00:00:27.268 --> 00:00:29.678
Grouping is organizational metadata.

00:00:29.956 --> 00:00:34.052
Credential resolution remains flat: a group does not create a new reference

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:34.969
namespace.

00:00:35.289 --> 00:00:37.944
Removing a group does not remove its credentials.

00:00:38.295 --> 00:00:42.477
Review administrator metadata changes carefully and verify the actual target

00:00:42.647 --> 00:00:44.596
and purpose before using a reference.

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:49.248
Create a clear reference for each target account or password transition.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.607
The username must match the account requested by the script.

00:00:52.906 --> 00:00:56.575
Use separate references for new local administrators and independent

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.370
nonempty passwords where validation requires them.

00:00:59.647 --> 00:01:01.684
A reference name is not a password.

00:01:01.971 --> 00:01:06.238
Validate resolution without printing secret values into logs, tickets or

00:01:06.323 --> 00:01:07.589
tutorial screenshots.

00:01:08.073 --> 00:01:12.936
Config Files remains the shared library for workflow, script, pipeline and

00:01:13.022 --> 00:01:14.139
recovery inputs.

00:01:14.445 --> 00:01:17.837
Open the intended file and inspect its targets before saving.

00:01:18.157 --> 00:01:19.964
Retain reviewed recovery versions.

00:01:20.248 --> 00:01:24.643
Organize files using datacenter and cluster groups, shared credential groups

00:01:24.813 --> 00:01:25.957
and purpose labels.

00:01:26.246 --> 00:01:30.108
Search and scoped workflow or pipeline pickers help narrow the list.

00:01:30.513 --> 00:01:35.505
Group labels do not rename a file, rewrite its Y A M L or change execution

00:01:35.676 --> 00:01:36.330
references.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.355
Choose the exact saved filename and confirm its content before execution.

00:01:41.658 --> 00:01:45.882
Restoring or editing a file changes desired input; it does not reverse

00:01:45.967 --> 00:01:47.098
target-side changes.

00:01:47.418 --> 00:01:51.514
If the file belongs to a reviewed recovery baseline, capture and review a

00:01:51.556 --> 00:01:53.426
new revision when its content changes.

00:01:53.923 --> 00:01:57.656
In YAML Studio choose the correct template family and generator.

00:01:57.976 --> 00:02:02.030
Complete the fields, generate the document and inspect validation, mapping

00:02:02.286 --> 00:02:04.045
and adapter-readiness findings.

00:02:04.397 --> 00:02:08.109
Resolve missing references or unsupported properties before saving.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:13.399
A successful YAML save is not execution approval, a live connection test or

00:02:13.442 --> 00:02:14.679
a completed deployment.

00:02:14.935 --> 00:02:18.170
Open the corresponding execution workflow for those next steps.

00:02:18.581 --> 00:02:23.360
Before execution, compare the saved YAML, action, target and credential

00:02:23.573 --> 00:02:25.536
references with the approved change.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.056
Approval can be bound to exact content and filename.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:32.326
Editing the document afterward can invalidate that binding.

00:02:32.588 --> 00:02:35.489
Never loosen policy to make changed content run.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:39.884
Keep sanitized configuration hashes and job identifiers so another operator

00:02:40.055 --> 00:02:43.626
can reconcile what was requested and what actually executed.
